WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:05.360
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I’m going to&nbsp;
explain a horror drama film called “The B4d S33d.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.400
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.400
At the beginning of the movie, we see a&nbsp;
nine-year-old girl named Emma Grossman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:21.440
watching a cat drowning in a fountain through her&nbsp;
room’s window. She closes the blinds, and goes on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.160
with her morning routine, showing no remorse to&nbsp;
the drowning cat. Emma lives with her widowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:31.600
father named David Grossman. She is an excellent&nbsp;
student and a well-mannered kid. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.800
she seems to have no human emotions. That day&nbsp;
at breakfast, Emma tells him of her ambition to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:42.000
win a citizenship award at school. As the&nbsp;
two talk, Emma’s aunt, Angela, comes in.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.600
She informs David of a new babysitter she has&nbsp;
found for Emma. It turns out that Emma’s previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.480
babysitter suffered an "unfortunate accident".&nbsp;
As they talk, Emma points out the dead cat in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.240
the fountain. David brings the cat out, but Emma&nbsp;
seems void of any emotions about its death.
&nbsp;

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:03.680
That day at school, a wasp scares the children&nbsp;
as they study. As the students retreat in fear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.680
Emma bravely takes a glass and captures the&nbsp;
wasp to let it fly outside the window.
&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:14.160
Meanwhile, David interviews a babysitter named&nbsp;
Chloe. He likes her portfolio of work, so he hires&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.080
her. Chloe seems to be interested in David.
Back at school, Emma’s classmate, Katie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:25.520
is playing when she bumps into Emma who helps her&nbsp;
get up. Their teacher watches the events unfold.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.240
It looks as if Emma is trying to be compassionate&nbsp;
to win the citizenship award. That night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.080
Emma practises smiling in front of the mirror. 
The following day is the award day. David dresses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:40.560
up Emma and drives her to school. All the&nbsp;
parents and students are seated in the audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:46.160
when the teacher announces that Milo has won the&nbsp;
citizenship award. Emma is beyond disappointed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.480
When David talks to Emma about Milo’s win,&nbsp;
she says that she was the one who deserved it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:55.200
and begins insulting Milo. She apologizes&nbsp;
when David looks at her disapprovingly.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.240
Sometime later, when no one is watching, Emma&nbsp;
takes Milo to show him a cliff nearby.
&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:06.960
When Milo suggests returning, Emma walks towards&nbsp;
him, and the screen goes blank. Later, when Milo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.440
parents ask her if she has seen him, she lies&nbsp;
and says she hasn’t seen him since the bonfire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.200
Suddenly, two girls come running from somewhere,&nbsp;
screaming for help. All the parents run to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.160
Milo has fallen off the cliff and drowned in the&nbsp;
ocean. His father carries his washed-up body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:27.280
and tries giving him CPR; but Milo is dead. 
The following morning at breakfast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.080
David asks Emma how she feels, but she completely&nbsp;
ignores the fact her friend died the day before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.880
Later, the new babysitter, Chloe,&nbsp;
comes to the house. That night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:41.440
David isn’t home. Emma finds Chloe in David’s&nbsp;
room stealing some of David’s medicines. 
&nbsp;

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.600
Later as they watch movies, Emma&nbsp;
confronts her about the drugs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:50.560
She promises to not tell David if Chloe does what&nbsp;
she wants. Emma then orders her to get her an ice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.000
cream. Chloe calls the little girl a bitch, but&nbsp;
does what she says. The following day is Milo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:02.160
memorial. After the ceremony, everyone is crying&nbsp;
except for Emma. David talks to Milo’s parents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:07.040
and finds out that the medal is missing. They&nbsp;
assume that it sank in the ocean. Just then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.240
Emma begins to cry too. It is as if she is&nbsp;
pretending to be sad in front of Milo’s parents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:15.840
When they come back home, David is&nbsp;
worried about Emma's behaviour. 
&nbsp;

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.760
When he folds Emma’s laundry that day, we see&nbsp;
that Milo’s medal is hidden under Emma’s mattress.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.280
David looks through the pictures of the&nbsp;
award day, and finds several pictures of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.520
Emma glaring at Milo. He suspects that his&nbsp;
death has to do something with Emma. 
&nbsp;

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:35.600
Later that day, Emma’s teacher ,Mrs Ellis, and a&nbsp;
police officer visit David to talk about Milo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.400
death. Mrs. Ellis claims that someone had seen&nbsp;
Emma with Milo in the cliff before his death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:45.840
Emma listens to their conversation from the door.&nbsp;
She fakes falling on a vase and hurting herself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.760
to stop the adults from talking. Seeing that Emma&nbsp;
is hurt, Mrs. Ellis and the officer leave. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:57.280
taking care of Emma’s wound, David asks her if she&nbsp;
was with Milo in the cliff, but Emma denies. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:02.160
he reveals that Mrs. Ellis said she was, Emma gets&nbsp;
agitated and yells that Mrs. Ellis hates her. 
&nbsp;

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.400
The following day, Chloe goes to their&nbsp;
side house where David is working.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:11.440
She asks him if she can smoke there, but David&nbsp;
denies, saying that the place has too many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:16.640
inflammable liquids. Right after, Chloe takes&nbsp;
Emma to the street to play with her scooter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:21.600
While they are at it, the two see Mrs. Ellis’s&nbsp;
car in front of Milo’s home. She is talking to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:26.720
Milo’s mother. Chloe says that they are building&nbsp;
a case against Emma. She knows that Emma did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:31.760
something to Milo. However, the little girl acts&nbsp;
like she doesn’t know what Chloe is talking about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:36.800
When they come back home, they continue the&nbsp;
conversation. Chloe tells Emma that if they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:41.680
find out what happened to Milo, they will sit&nbsp;
Emma in an electric chair. This scares Emma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:46.960
but she still doesn’t admit to doing anything.
Later that day, Chloe is looking for Emma around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.040
the house, when we notice the wasp nest that&nbsp;
had been in the ceiling of the outhouse is gone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:57.440
Then, we see Mrs. Ellis drive away from Milo’s&nbsp;
home. As she drives, a wasp distracts her which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:02.400
almost causes an accident. She continues to&nbsp;
drive when the camera pans to the back seat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.120
The wasp’s nest lies there. Emma has put the&nbsp;
nest in the car to try and kill her teacher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.400
Back at home, Chloe finds Milo’s medal under&nbsp;
Emma’s mattress. She hangs it in a lamp in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.520
David’s dresser so that Emma can be caught. David&nbsp;
is in his bathroom, when Emma comes to his room&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:22.320
and sees the medal. She gets it off the lamp&nbsp;
and hides it behind her, but David notices.  
&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:27.360
He brings her back to her room, and confronts her&nbsp;
about it. Emma lies and makes up a story about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.080
Milo giving the medal to her as they played.&nbsp;
David goes for a drive to take mind off this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:36.640
when he sees a car crashed on the side of&nbsp;
the road. He also calls Angela and asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.960
her to find Emma a therapist. David begins&nbsp;
to get nightmares about Emma and Milo. 
&nbsp;

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.040
The following day, Emma confronts Chloe about&nbsp;
her putting the Medal there. She is furious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:51.760
Just then, David comes downstairs and asks&nbsp;
Emma to come with him. He takes her to Milo’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.720
home to return the medal back to his mom. She is&nbsp;
confused, but thankful that she brought it back.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:02.880
She then informs them about Mrs. Ellis‘s death.&nbsp;
She had had a car accident because of the wasps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.760
David is surprised. Emma begins to cry, claiming&nbsp;
that Mrs. Ellis was her favorite teacher.
&nbsp;

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.880
However, on their way home, Emma seems to&nbsp;
have forgotten about Mrs. Ellis’s death and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:18.640
talks about baking cookies with Chloe. David is&nbsp;
unsettled by Emma’s behaviour. Later, as David&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:23.600
is working in the outhouse, he notices that the&nbsp;
wasp’s nest is gone. He suspects his daughter for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:28.880
Mrs. Ellis’s death. The following day is Emma’s&nbsp;
first appointment with her therapist, Dr. March.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:34.800
She and Emma have a long chat. After the session,&nbsp;
the doctor tells David that Emma is like any other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:40.560
normal child; Emma even fooled a psychiatrist!
When the two come back home, David comes across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.560 --> 00:06:46.720
Chloe sunbathing in her sports bra. He asks her&nbsp;
to go to Emma. As Chloe and Emma talk, she tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.120
the little girl that David was looking at her&nbsp;
seductively earlier. She also adds that she can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:57.200
be her step mother. Furious, Emma screams at her&nbsp;
to stay away from her dad. That night, Emma asks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:02.840
David if he likes Chloe. David is confused. She&nbsp;
also reveals about Chloe wanting to be her step&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:08.080
mother. However, David is late for a date, so he&nbsp;
leaves without giving her much of an explanation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.840
Some time later, Chloe hears a noise as she&nbsp;
is watching TV. She goes looking for Emma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.840 --> 00:07:18.560
but cannot find her anywhere. She looks at the out&nbsp;
house through the window and sees a shadow there.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:22.640
She goes out to look for her.
When she gets into the outhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:28.400
the door closes. She tries to open it but it seems&nbsp;
to be locked from outside. Just then a fire starts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:33.520
spreading on the floor. Chloe sees Emma watch her&nbsp;
through the window. She tries to hit her but the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:38.800
fire indulges her, killing her eventually. David&nbsp;
comes home to the firefighters and paramedics in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:43.520
his house; they tell him about Chloe’s death.&nbsp;
Emma has been taken to an official's home;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:48.400
he finally gets to Emma and hugs her. 
That night, David comes to Emma’s room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:53.120
He sits down in front of her and lovingly asks&nbsp;
her if she hurt Milo. He assures her that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:57.760
will do anything he can to help her, but she&nbsp;
has to tell him the truth. Emma finally admits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:02.320
that she pushed Milo off the cliff. She makes an&nbsp;
excuse by saying that he was going to report her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:07.360
for taking his medal.She then casually says that&nbsp;
she won’t do it again. David is horrified.
&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:13.840
He then asks her about Mrs Levia, Emma’s previous&nbsp;
babysitter. She reveals that she pushed her down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.840 --> 00:08:18.560
the stairs because Mrs. Levia grabbed her hand.&nbsp;
She then claims that Levia should have been more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:24.160
careful. Emma gets progressively aggressive as&nbsp;
she talks. When asked about what she did to Chloe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:29.440
she yells at David and blames Chloe for trying&nbsp;
to be her stepmother. David is anxious; he cannot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:34.640
believe that his little daughter can commit such&nbsp;
a horrible crime. The following morning, the town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:39.440
Sheriff calls David and says he wants to meet&nbsp;
Emma. However, David makes an excuse about her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:44.480
being sick. He then takes her to their lake house&nbsp;
far away. Their housekeeper welcomes them. 
&nbsp;

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:50.000
Later that day, the Sheriff calls David again to&nbsp;
inform him that the fire was set deliberately by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:55.120
someone, but they don’t know who. Seeing that&nbsp;
his daughter might get caught, he is anxious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:59.600
David has a gun with him at the house. He looks&nbsp;
at it now and then thinking if he can put it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:04.960
to use to solve the situation. The following&nbsp;
day, as David is asleep, Emma comes into his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.680
room and kisses him. She closes all the windows&nbsp;
and turns all the gas stoves on in an attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:15.120
to kill her father. Emma then goes by the lake&nbsp;
and stays there. Just then, David wakes up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.920
smells the gas filling up the house. He quickly&nbsp;
opens the windows, and turns the stoves off. 
&nbsp;

00:09:20.720 --> 00:09:24.960
He sees Emma outside at the lake, and&nbsp;
realizes that she has tried to kill him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.840
He walks up to her and asks her why she did that.&nbsp;
Emma replies that if something happened to him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:34.480
she gets to go live with her aunt, Angela,&nbsp;
who actually likes her. David holds her hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:40.240
and calmly takes her into the house. Then, we&nbsp;
see David crush his medicines. Later, he brings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:45.600
Emma a cup of hot chocolate. The two drink the hot&nbsp;
chocolate together and David tucks her to sleep.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.560
When he comes back to his room, he calls Angela&nbsp;
and tells her everything about Emma’s wrongdoings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:55.360
but she doesn’t believe him. He apologizes to&nbsp;
Angela and vaguely tells her that he has no other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:00.240
options. It turns out that David had added drugs&nbsp;
in Emma’s hot chocolate in order to overdose her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:04.080
so that she doesn’t kill more people.&nbsp;
But he doesnt tell Angela this.
 
&nbsp;

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.640
That night when he is asleep, Emma enters&nbsp;
his room. She holds a gun in his hand and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:14.400
points it at himself. She fires, but misses,&nbsp;
sending the bullet to the pillow beside David.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:19.280
The noise wakes him up and he asks her how is she&nbsp;
still alive. Emma replies that she had switched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:24.000
her hot chocolate with David’s. Seeing that she&nbsp;
was about to kill him, David leaps to snatch the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:30.000
gun from her hand. Emma quickly takes his phone&nbsp;
and calls 911. She then runs away to the bathroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.160
as David follows her with the intention to&nbsp;
kill her. Emma tells the 911 operator that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:38.000
her father is trying to kill her. 
David breaks open the bathroom door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:42.560
and points his gun at Emma. Just then, the&nbsp;
housekeeper appears behind him with his rifle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:48.240
When David is about to kill Emma, he shoots him&nbsp;
instead. Emma watches as her father falls down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:54.080
to the ground and dies. The police arrive too.
Cut to the following morning, Aunt Angela arrives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:58.800
at the scene. She tells Emma that her&nbsp;
dad was probably sick. The movie ends as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.480
we see Emma hug Angela and smirk, with&nbsp;
a cold predatory look on her face.
